DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The vvttffoonnttccvvtt utility reads source font files in either BDF or Unifont
     HEX format and outputs a file in one of the available output formats.

     HEX format files (_n_o_r_m_a_l___f_o_n_t and _b_o_l_d___f_o_n_t) must have the file extension
     _._h_e_x.

     The following options are available:

     --ff _f_o_r_m_a_t       Specify the output format.  Available formats are:

                     ccoommpprreesssseedd--ssoouurrccee  C source with font data compressed by
                                        using LZ4 compression method.

                     ffoonntt               A binary font file (default).

                     ssoouurrccee             C source.

                     The output in C source is intended to be used to embed
                     the font into program binary.

                     The binary font file is for use by vt(4).

     --hh _h_e_i_g_h_t       Set font height.  The default is 16.  Font height is set
                     automatically for BDF files and for HEX files that have a
                           # Height: _h_e_i_g_h_t
                     comment before any font data.

     --nn              Do not apply output filtering with C source output.

     --oo _o_u_t_p_u_t___f_i_l_e  Specify the name for the output file.

     --vv              Display verbose statistics about the converted font.

     --ww _w_i_d_t_h        Set font width.  The default is 8.  Font width is set au‐
                     tomatically for BDF files and for HEX files that have a
                           # Width: _w_i_d_t_h
                     comment before any font data.

